# --accept-flake-config, because direnv cannot answer a question. flake.nix
# declares nixConfig.extra-substituters, and nix asks for consent per SETTING
# against the whole value string — measured 2026-09-02, it asks even for values
# already present in /etc/nix/nix.custom.conf. In an interactive shell that is a
# y/N prompt; here it is a hang, and the only visible symptom is direnv's
# "is taking a while to execute. Use CTRL-C to give up."
#
# Scope is narrow on purpose: the flag applies to THIS repo's own flake, the same
# thing whose justfile you already run. It is not `accept-flake-config` in
# nix.conf, which would accept any flake's substituters silently.
use flake . --no-pure-eval --accept-flake-config
